message.content:
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All new public API functions will follow existing fabric-config library naming, parameter, and return value conventions to maintain consistency with the current codebase.",
    "The bulk CLI tool will reuse the existing fabric-config library for all configuration manipulation logic, only adding CLI parsing, I/O handling, and network interaction functionality.",
    "All new functions will include upfront input validation to fail fast and return clear, actionable error messages for invalid inputs.",
    "The RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses and RemoveKafkaBrokers functions will be implemented as irreversible operations to prevent accidental re-introduction of deprecated configuration fields.",
    "Consenter removal functions will require an exact match of all 4 identifying fields (host, port, client TLS certificate, server TLS certificate) to avoid partial or incorrect removals.",
    "The bulk CLI tool will use the standard Fabric connection profile format for peer/orderer connectivity and configuration block fetching, leveraging existing Fabric SDK parsing logic where possible.",
    "All new example code will be added to the existing examples directory of the fabric-config repository, following the structure and style of existing examples.",
    "Certificate-related MSP update functions will include PEM format validation to ensure only valid certificates are added to the configuration."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The existing fabric-config library codebase (version referenced in the specification) is fully accessible for modification, with no breaking changes to existing public APIs required for the new features.",
    "All required Hyperledger Fabric network components (peer, orderer binaries, test network) are available in the development environment for integration and end-to-end testing.",
    "The Fabric connection profile format specified in the user stories is fully compatible with existing Fabric SDK/CLI parsing logic, requiring no modifications to core Fabric components.",
    "No changes to the underlying Hyperledger Fabric core protocol or consensus logic are required for the implemented features; all changes are limited to the fabric-config library and the new bulk CLI tool.",
    "The existing unit and integration test suite for the fabric-config library is available and can be extended to cover new functionality, with no need to rewrite or modify existing tests.",
    "The signing identities JSON format specified in the bulk CLI tool requirements is compatible with existing Fabric signing identity parsing logic."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Add Consortium API Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the public API function to add a new consortium to the consortiums group, add input validation to reject adding a consortium with no associated orgs, update existing code examples to demonstrate the correct flow of adding a consortium followed by adding orgs to it, write unit tests for the new function and edge case.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Signing-Independent Config Update Envelope Function",
      "activity_description": "Implement a new function that generates a cb.ConfigUpdateEnvelope without requiring pre-provided signing identities, add input validation for the config update payload, write unit tests for the new function.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Legacy Orderer Address Removal Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses function for the top-level channel group, add validation to block updates to the deprecated top-level OrdererAddresses field, modify genesis block generation logic to exclude the top-level OrdererAddresses field and require orderer orgs to define their own endpoints, update relevant examples, write unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - KafkaBrokers Removal Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function to entirely remove the KafkaBrokers section from orderer configuration, add an example demonstrating Kafka to EtcdRaft migration using this function, write unit tests for the removal function.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5 - EtcdRaft Consenter Add/Remove Functions",
      "activity_description": "Implement AddConsenter and RemoveConsenter functions for etcdraft orderer configuration, enforce that consenter removal matches all 4 fields (host, port, client TLS cert, server TLS cert) to avoid partial matches, add input validation for consenter parameters, update relevant examples, write unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 9
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Bulk Channel CLI Tool Development",
      "activity_description": "Develop the CLI tool that consumes the fabric-config library, implement JSON parsing for batch update files, connection profiles, and signing identities, implement support for all required operations (cert expiry, V1-V2 migration, add/remove/replace anchor peers, consenter operations), implement dry-run mode that outputs the calculated config update, implement config block fetching via the provided connection profile, implement config update submission to the orderer, add error handling for unsupported operations and invalid inputs, add example JSON input files and usage documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Individual Orderer Config Update Functions",
      "activity_description": "Implement the set of individual orderer configuration update functions (SetMaxMessageCount, SetAbsoluteMaxBytes, SetPreferredMaxBytes, SetBatchTimeout, SetMaxChannels, SetConsensusType, EtcdRaft metadata update functions, SetConsensusState), ensure all functions persist existing values for unmodified fields, update examples to demonstrate both the legacy Get/Set configuration flow and the new individual function flow, write unit tests for all new functions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 18
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Individual MSP Update Functions",
      "activity_description": "Implement individual MSP update functions for OrdererOrgGroup, ApplicationOrgGroup, and ConsortiumOrgGroup (AddRootCert, RemoveRootCert, AddIntermediateCert, RemoveIntermediateCert, AddAdminCert, RemoveAdminCert, AddCRL, RemoveCRL, AddOUIdentifier, RemoveOUIdentifier, SetCryptoConfig, AddTLSRootCert, RemoveTLSRootCert, AddTLSIntermediateCert, RemoveTLSIntermediateCert, SetClientOUIdentifier, SetPeerOUIdentifier, SetAdminOUIdentifier, SetOrdererOUIdentifier, EnableNodeOUs, DisableNodeOUs), add PEM format validation for all certificate-related inputs, update examples to demonstrate both the legacy Get/Set MSP flow and the new individual function flow, write unit tests for all new functions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Integration and End-to-End Testing",
      "activity_description": "Perform integration testing of all new API functions against a test Fabric network, test the bulk CLI tool end-to-end with all supported operations including dry-run mode, verify error handling for invalid inputs and unsupported operations, fix any bugs identified during testing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and Example Updates",
      "activity_description": "Update the fabric-config library API reference documentation to include all new functions, update the CLI tool usage guide, add formal usage examples for all new features including the Kafka to EtcdRaft migration and V1 to V2 channel migration flows.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 128
  }
}

